This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u),
  \quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|u|^2dx=c^2,\quad u\in H^2(\mathbb{R}^4),
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} where $\beta>0$, $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$, $0<\mu<2$, and $f$ and $F$ are defined as in the paper. Under certain conditions on the parameters $\beta$, $\lambda$, and $\mu$, we establish the existence and uniqueness of a normalized ground state solution for this equation.

